{
  "statement": "Trustworthiness is critical in a bookkeeping system to ensure data protection and integrity. TRU-01 mandates encryption to secure financial transactions during transmission and storage, while TRU-02 implements role-based access control to prevent unauthorized access. TRU-03 ensures an immutable audit trail for accountability, and TRU-04 validates data input to protect against malicious entries. TRU-05 enhances security through two-factor authentication. TRU-06 requires comprehensive logging of user access for transparency, and TRU-07 limits data access based on user roles. However, logging (TRU-06) may conflict with efficiency requirements (EFF-07) regarding logging delays, and encryption (TRU-01) may introduce processing overhead affecting performance (EFF-01).",
